# Security & Audit Logging

## Security Baseline
- Auth: short-lived JWT access tokens + rotating refresh tokens (reuse detection), stored in httpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookies.
- Authorization: RBAC (extendable to ABAC) via guards; roles and permissions stored in DB/config — never hardcoded.
- Rate limiting (`@nestjs/throttler`, Redis-backed) with limits from config.
- `helmet`, strict CORS (origins from config), CSRF protection for cookie-based flows.
- class-validator DTOs on every input; global ValidationPipe with `whitelist` and `forbidNonWhitelisted`.
- Follow OWASP Top 10. Never leak stack traces, internal errors, or secrets. Secrets only from env/secret manager, never committed.

## Audit Log (mandatory for ALL actions)
Every action is audited — no exceptions:
- All create/update/delete operations in every domain.
- Auth events: login, logout, failed login, token refresh, password/MFA changes.
- Authorization changes: role/permission grants and revocations.
- Sensitive reads and exports, admin actions, config/feature-flag changes, system/job-initiated changes.

Implementation:
- A dedicated `audit` domain owns the audit store; other modules emit audit events through its public interface/events — never write the table directly.
- Captured automatically via a global interceptor + domain events so no action can be missed; explicit `@Audit()` decorator for custom metadata.
- Each record: UUID, timestamp (UTC), actor ID + type (user/system/service), action, entity type + ID, before/after diff, outcome (success/failure + reason), IP, user agent, correlation ID.
- Append-only and immutable: no updates/deletes (enforced at DB level via permissions/triggers).
- Written reliably via the outbox/queue so audit never blocks or is lost.
- PII redacted per config; retention period, partitioning (by time), and archival are configurable.
- Indexed for querying by actor, entity, action, and time range; exposed via a permission-protected read API.
